==== Description of expected options:
Evolve a binary black hole using the Generalized Harmonic formulation


Options:
  ResourceInfo:
    type=ResourceInfo
    Options for allocating resources. This information will be used when
    placing Array and Singleton parallel components on the requested
    resources.

  EvolutionSystem:
    The system of hyperbolic PDEs

  Amr:
    Options for adaptive mesh refinement (AMR)

  DomainCreator:
    type=DomainCreator
    The domain to create initially

  Observers:
    Options for recording data

  BbhCompletionCriteria:
    Options controlling inspiral termination based on global BBH criteria.

  InterpolationTargets:
    Options for interpolation targets

  Cce:
    Options for the Cce evolution system

  Parallelization:
    Options related to parallelization aspects of the simulation.

  ApparentHorizons:
    Options for apparent horizon finders

  Interpolator:
    Options related to the Interpolator parallel component

  ControlSystems:
    Options for all control systems used in a simulation.

  Evolution:
    Options for the time evolution

  SpatialDiscretization:
    Options controlling the spatial discretization of the PDE system.

    In a DG-subcell hybrid scheme subgroups would hold options for the DG and
    FD/FV method used. For example, the choice of basis functions for the DG
    scheme would be specified.

  InitialData:
    type=InitialData
    Options for initial data of evolution system

  EventsAndTriggersAtCheckpoints:
    type=EventsAndTriggers
    Events to run at triggers

  EventsAndTriggersAtSlabs:
    type=EventsAndTriggers
    Events to run at triggers

  EventsAndTriggersAtSteps:
    type=EventsAndTriggers
    Events to run at triggers

  PhaseChangeAndTriggers:
    type=[TriggerAndPhaseChanges, ...]
    A collection of pairs of triggers and collections of phase change objects
    to determine runtime phase control-flow decisions. The order of the phase
    change objects determines the order of the requests processed by the Main
    chare during phase change arbitration.

  EventsRunAtCleanup:
    Options related to running events on failure.  This is generally intended
    for dumping volume data to diagnose failure reasons.

  EventsAndDenseTriggers:
    type=EventsAndDenseTriggers
    Events to run at arbitrary times

